This is a Vite + React app serving smarthome dashboards. The smart home is Homey-based. It uses the `homey-api` npm package and an auth token for authorization to Homey. The app has two pages for two dashboards: one in the 1st floor living room (`/`), and one in the 1st floor entre (`/entre`). Both dashboards run on Raspberry Pis. The living-room Pi also runs this app (Express serves the Vite `build/` output plus `/api` routes).

Requires Node.js LTS via nvm (`.nvmrc` = `lts/*`, `package.json` engines `^24.19.0`). The smart home also posts data to an MQTT server.

## Tooling

- Build/dev: Vite (`npm start` / `npm run build`)
- Production server: `npm run start:production` (Express on `PORT`, default 80)
- API during Vite dev: `npm run start:api` (port 3080; Vite proxies `/api`)
- Lint/format/test: `npm run lint`, `npm run format`, `npm run test`
- Health check: `npm run verify` (expects HTTP 200 on `/`, `/entre`, `/api/read/temperature/loft`)
